#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A one-laptop Yellowback v3 regtest network, ARMED when `up` returns, with a seat left empty.

The plain devnet (`up`, today's behaviour) is eight nodes: node 0 the funded wallet, node 1
stock, nodes 2-4 signalling pools with fixed payout addresses, nodes 5-7 attestor nodes that
register (10 YEC, 200 blocks) and arm the layer, each with a real `yellowback-attest attest`
beside it and one `subscribe` beside node 0, all on the `dir` transport. `--no-attest` gives
back the five-node v2 devnet.

`up --role {user,attestor,pool}` (docs/plans/role-based-regtest-plan.md) is the same chain
with **one seat deliberately left unautomated** and the world kept moving around it: eleven
nodes, a heartbeat that mines a block every N seconds on the automated pools only, a price
that walks, and a simulated population of personas (`yellowback-sim`) minting, redeeming,
trading and liquidating on nodes 9 and 10.

    node  0  you (`user`) or the funding + subscriber node   5-7  attestors, automated
          1  stock, no -yellowback                          8    4th attestor, or YOU (`attestor`)
          2-3 pools, automated                              9    the simulated population
          4  pool, automated, or YOU (`pool`)               10   the simulated liquidator

YELLOWBACK_DEVNET_DIR and YELLOWBACK_DEVNET_PORTSEED (or PORTBASE) let two devnets run side by
side; YELLOWBACK_WALLET_BIN and YELLOWBACK_ATTEST_BIN name the two binaries.

Commands: up [--role R] [--agents] [--no-attest] [--lean] [--no-heartbeat] [--no-walk] [--no-sim]
[--seed N], check, status, mine N [node], heartbeat {start|stop|rate N|status},
price USD | price --walk [start|stop] [--drift PCT] [--vol PCT] [--tick SEC] | price --shock=PCT,
attestor N {stop|start|price USD}, pool N {configure|signal on|off|quote start|stop},
sim {start|stop|stats}, notice VAULTTXID, scenario [NAME], report, wallet [--node N],
cli [--node N | --datadir N] [-- args], down [--wipe].
"""
